Drop the `umask 077` around Autoconf's config.status scratch directory.

On HarmonyOS/HMDFS a directory's permission bits are rewritten by the file
system: a normal `mkdir` yields 0o2771 (setgid forced, still writable) while
`umask 077 && mktemp -d` yields 0o2700, whose owning uid is the hmdfs account
id rather than the calling uid, so the "other" class (---) is the one that
applies and even the creating process cannot write into its own scratch
directory.  configure/config.status then aborts with
  ./config.status: line 839: ./confXXXXXX/subs1.awk: Permission denied
  config.status: error: could not setup config files machinery
Measured on this image (uid maps to hmdfs account uid, not the process uid):
  mkdir mode 0700            -> 0o2771  WRITE OK
  mkdir + chmod 0700         -> 0o2771  WRITE OK
  mktemp -d                  -> 0o2771  WRITE OK
  (umask 077 && mktemp -d)   -> 0o2700  WRITE FAIL Permission denied
The scratch tree only ever holds generated substitution scripts for the current
build, created and removed by the same process, so the tightened umask buys
nothing here.  Same workaround as archives/a/aaphoto/0.45 and the
abiword-plugin-* recipes.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -20067,12 +20067,12 @@
 # Create a (secure) tmp directory for tmp files.
 
 {
-  tmp=`(umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
+  tmp=`mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX" 2>/dev/null` &&
   test -d "$tmp"
 }  ||
 {
   tmp=./conf$$-$RANDOM
-  (umask 077 && mkdir "$tmp")
+  mkdir "$tmp"
 } || as_fn_error $? "cannot create a temporary directory in ." "$LINENO" 5
 ac_tmp=$tmp
 
